.TH CLIPBRIDGE 1 clipbridge\-VERSION
.SH NAME
clipbridge \- universal clipboard bridge & background daemon powered by unipaste
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipbridge
.RB [ \-w1pruv ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR table ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR link ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipbridge
connects desktop graphical clipboards to the \fBunipaste\fR formatting engine.
It intercepts rich clipboard payloads (such as HTML copied from Slack, Teams, or browsers)
and automatically upgrades the fallback plain text on the system clipboard using
\fBunipaste\fR's table alignment, list hierarchy, and code block formatting.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-w
Watch the system clipboard continuously in the background (default).
.TP
.B \-1
Perform a single clipboard synchronization and exit immediately (ideal for hotkey bindings).
.TP
.B \-p
Print formatted clipboard text directly to standard output.
.SH FORMATTING OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " mode"
Output mode: \fBplain\fR (default), \fBmarkdown\fR, or \fBterminal\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " table"
Table format: \fBgrid\fR (default), \fBmarkdown\fR, \fBtsv\fR, or \fBsimple\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l " link"
Link format: \fBbracket\fR (default), \fBinline\fR, \fBtext\fR, or \fBfootnote\fR.
.TP
.B \-u
Use Unicode box-drawing characters for tables.
.TP
.B \-r
Emit Windows CRLF (\\r\\n) line endings.
.TP
.B \-v
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Display help message and exit.
